  "instructions": "Match each whole Arabic word with its Latin reading. Each match joins the two scripts and plays the Arabic word.",
  "notation": {
    "system": "arabic-learning-romanization-v1",
    "help": "Reading key: ā, ī, ū are long vowels; sh as in ship, th as in thin, dh as in this; kh and gh are throat sounds. ḥ is a deeper h; ṣ, ḍ, ṭ, ẓ are emphatic sounds; ʿ marks ʿayn and ʾ a glottal stop. Doubled consonants are held longer. These are isolated verb readings with their written endings. Use the Arabic audio too. Readings await native review."
  },
